sieve-filter-v2
; A melody that comes home: the last event is a note on the tonic (any octave), at least `hold`
; long, so a track resolves rather than stopping mid-phrase. For notes104 (durations e q h w).
; The state is whether the last event so far would end it well.
id        melody-ending
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes104
describe  The last note is the tonic, held at least so long.
param     tonic  choice  C C,C#,D,D#,E,F,F#,G,G#,A,A#,B the note to end on
param     hold   choice  e e,q,h,w the shortest the last note may be

states    2
start     0
accept    1
for s 0 1
  for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
    t {s} @{d} 0
    for p 1 {PITCHES}
      if {(LOW + p - 1) % 12 == tonic && d >= hold}
        t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} 1
      else
        t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} 0
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
